---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const recoverRequirementsResult = await recoverRequirements(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const generateConceptsResult = await generateConcepts(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverRequirementsResult.accepted);
const planProductionResult = await planProduction(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, generateConceptsResult.accepted);
const calculateQuoteResult = await calculateQuote(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planProductionResult.accepted);
const confirmScopeResult = await confirmScope(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, calculateQuoteResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { recoverRequirements: recoverRequirementsResult, generateConcepts: generateConceptsResult, planProduction: planProductionResult, calculateQuote: calculateQuoteResult, confirmScope: confirmScopeResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...recoverRequirementsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...generateConceptsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planProductionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...calculateQuoteResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...confirmScopeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...recoverRequirementsResult.checks, ...generateConceptsResult.checks, ...planProductionResult.checks, ...calculateQuoteResult.checks, ...confirmScopeResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A customer supplies approximate dimensions: label the quote provisional until confirmed measurements arrive. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (label the quote provisional until confirmed measurements arrive.) through the existing stage result for FabricationRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior FabricationRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A finish sample differs from a screen rendering: require acceptance of the physical or approved reference. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require acceptance of the physical or approved reference.) through the existing stage result for FabricationRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior FabricationRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Material prices expire: revalidate the quote before commitment. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (revalidate the quote before commitment.) through the existing stage result for FabricationRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior FabricationRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A design change affects tooling: update route and cost together. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (update route and cost together.) through the existing stage result for FabricationRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior FabricationRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — The shop lacks a required certification: disclose the limit and route specialist work appropriately. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (disclose the limit and route specialist work appropriately.) through the existing stage result for FabricationRequirement; preserve exact source/version and the prior FabricationRequirement, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, recoverRequirements: recoverRequirementsResult, generateConcepts: generateConceptsResult, planProduction: planProductionResult, calculateQuote: calculateQuoteResult, confirmScope: confirmScopeResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
